le, “你再仔细检查代码” -> trace the entire binding/deploy chain, not merely the Y\r\nAML value. [Task 2]\r\n- when the user emphasizes “A B 都是同一个账户同一个环境” or asks “你测试，我已经部署到dev了” -> run the deployed start\r\n→list→revoke→list chain and give the actual `securityGuardEnabled` evidence before attributing a stale UI to client cac\r\nhing. [Task 2][Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Guard lives in `yopu-trade-order`: `shipOrder` transitions 4→5 and `deliverOrder` 5→7; auto-revoke in `deliverOrder` \r\nmust be best-effort so guard failure cannot break completion. Use `TradeUserAuthContext.getUserId()`, set cross-user sh\r\nard with `TradeOrderUserShardContext` in try/finally, and expose only `GET /v1/trade/order/guard/location` publicly. De\r\nployed dev proved start→list true→revoke→list false. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- A token is valid only when `guard:meta:{token}` exists, current HMAC verification passes, it is unrevoked, and it rem\r\nains the order’s current mapping. Separate 51001 from 51004 and `200 + valid:false`, then match the share link’s enviro\r\nnment to the environment that owns Redis; location reports refresh only `guard:loc`, never extend the 72h meta TTL. [Ta\r\nsk 2]\r\n- `securityGuardEnabled` is recomputed by `batchIsActive(orderNos)` from Redis; revoke deletes the order mapping and li\r\nst POST is not covered by the gateway’s GET cache. If an app still shows enabled after a confirmed revoke, capture the \r\nlist response before debugging backend cache. [Task 2]\r\n- Query-rate increments must refresh the 60-second TTL every request. A no-TTL `guard:rlimit:q:{ip}` key accumulates pe\r\nrmanently. `vicp.fun` does not pass a real client IP, so the tunnel shares the default 10/min/IP quota; use internal ga\r\nteway IPs or redesign as IP+token / raise the test limit. [Task 2]\r\n- A newly created guard session must use its own `startedAt`; never return an old session’s timestamp merely because Re\r\ndis/DB history remains. Verify `durationSec` on the deployed dev order, not only unit tests. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- `GuardTokenUtil` once checked for a 16-character signature even though it emits full 64-hex HMAC -> keep `SIG_HEX_LEN\r\nGTH=64` aligned with token output and use constant-time comparison. [Task 1]\r\n- Adding a `GuardTokenServiceImpl` constructor dependency breaks direct unit-test construction -> update constructor ca\r\nlls and run module `test-compile` immediately. A deployed bug that persists may be a stale jar: GitLab deploy jobs are \r\nbranch-gated, so verify job branch and deployed commit. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / private-space agreement location-information clause\r\nscope: Maintain the 06 私密空间协议 with evidence-backed location wording and precise renumbering; use when policy text\r\n must match implemented GPS flows without overclaiming storage protections.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform and C:\\Users\\79873\\Desktop\\yeqian\\需求\\协议\\友圃\r\n协议文件—修0628; reuse_rule=the protocol paths/line numbers are document-version-specific; scope containment, preservat\r\nion, and implementation-to-wording checks are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Add the 06 agreement’s missing location-information chapter\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-18T11-13-16-vwJA-yopu_private_space_agreement_add_location_info_clause.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\works\r\npace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\18\\rollout-2026\r\n-08-18T19-13-16-01a01493-5a9c-7111-bbb7-aad0bb2a14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-18T11:20:24+00:00, thread_id=01a01493-5a\r\n9c-7111-bbb7-aad0bb2a14d2, success: targeted clause and numbering diff verified)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 06-友圃私密空间使用协议.md, 位置信息, GPS位置校验, PrivateSpaceServiceImpl.geoCheck, Haversine, distance-threshold-me\r\nters, OPEN_LATITUDE, OPEN_LONGITUDE, CRLF, KMS\r\n\r\n## Task 2: